title: Judiciary & Intelligence
subtitle: Courts, investigations and the Senate Bureau of Intelligence.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_law.svg
view-if: judiciary_timer <= 0 and chair_judiciary = "rc" and cardok_judiciary
on-arrival: {! Q.turn_actions += 1; Q.judiciary_timer = 3; Q.last_card_timer = 'judiciary'; SW.porkPick(Q, 'judiciary'); !}
new-page: true
on-display: {! SW.cardStuck(Q, this); !}

= Judiciary & Intelligence Committee

The Caucus chairs the Judiciary & Intelligence Committee: the Republic's courts, the Judicial Department and the Senate Bureau of Intelligence answer to it.

- @prosecute: Prosecute corruption.
- @ethics: Establish a Senate Ethics Commission.
- @intel: [? if sith_stage <= 2 : Order an intelligence review of the people who profited from the crises. ?][? if sith_stage = 3 : Order an intelligence review of the Senate's inner circle. ?][? if sith_stage = 4 : Order an intelligence review of [+ pal_title +]'s contacts. ?]
- @gunray: Press the case against Nute Gunray.
- @warrant: Prepare a Senate warrant for the Sith Lord.
- @bureau_reform: Reform the Senate bureaucracy.
- @civil_service: Put the Civil Service Act to the Senate.
- @amedda: Arrest Vice Chair Mas Amedda.
- @integrity: Create an Office of Public Integrity.
- @expel: Move to expel the Senate's most corrupt members.
- @oversight_act: Put the Intelligence Oversight Act to the Senate.
- @compor: Found the Commission for the Protection of the Republic.
- @hhc_investigate: Investigate the human-first groups.
- @syndicates: Break the syndicates.
- @patronage_1: Fill Coruscant's judgeships with friends.
- @patronage_2: Quietly close the investigations into friendly senators.
- @patronage_3: Lease listening posts from friendly worlds.
- @patronage_4: Appoint friendly sector magistrates on the Rim.
- @patronage_5: Drop the charges against friendly shipping magnates.
- @patronage_6: Give the intelligence contracts to friendly firms.
- @easy_discard
- @set_aside

@prosecute
view-if: corruption > 20
subtitle: −3 corruption; some blocs feel targeted.
on-arrival: corruption -= 3; mod_relation -= 3; guild_relation -= 3; faith += 0.5

Twelve senators and forty officials are indicted for bribery. Several of them were Caucus allies.

@ethics
view-if: not anti_corruption
subtitle: −1 political capital. A permanent safeguard against corruption, if the Senate agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt and guild_hold = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if guild_hold > 0 : The guilds whose money we took will not allow it. ?][? if guild_hold = 0 : Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.15, rim: 0.7, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.45, cis: 0.3}, true);
var push = SW.ethicsPush(Q);
if (push) for (var b in st) st[b] = SW.clamp(st[b] + push, 0, 1);
Q.eth_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', 'regulate', 'corruption']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Senate Ethics Commission Act', Q.eth_vote);
if (Q.eth_vote >= 50) { Q.anti_corruption = 1; Q.corruption -= 4; Q.faith += 2; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if anti_corruption : The Senate Ethics Commission is born, with real powers of audit. Corruption will be harder from now on. ?][? if not anti_corruption : Too many senators have too much to hide. The bill fails. ?]

@intel
view-if: intel_runs < 3
subtitle: [? if sith_stage <= 2 : +1 evidence. Whoever is behind them may notice. ?][? if sith_stage = 3 : +1 evidence, and one name off the shortlist. ?][? if sith_stage = 4 : +1 evidence. His people may notice, and so may he. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.evidence += 1; Q.intel_runs += 1;
Q.intel_cleared = '';
if (Q.sith_stage === 3) { var nx = SW.nextOpenSuspect(Q); if (nx) { SW.clearSuspect(Q, nx, 'review'); Q.intel_cleared = Q.suspect_last_name; } }
if (Q.sith_stage === 4) SW.riskAlarm(Q, 1, 0.4);
if (Math.random() < 0.15 + Q.grand_plan / 500) Q.leak_pending = 1;
!}

[? if sith_stage <= 2 : The Bureau's analysts map everyone who profited from the Republic's crises. A disturbing number of them lead to people who later died, disappeared or became very rich, and the money always seems to end up on Coruscant. ?][? if sith_stage = 3 and intel_cleared : The Bureau's analysts take the Senate's inner circle apart, one office at a time. [+ suspect_last_finding +] [+ intel_cleared +] is not the Sith Lord. ?][? if sith_stage = 3 and not intel_cleared : The Bureau's analysts go over the Senate's inner circle once more. Nothing new. ?][? if sith_stage = 4 : The Bureau's analysts map [+ pal_title +]'s contacts. A disturbing number of them lead to people who later died, disappeared or became very rich. ?]

@expel
view-if: integrity_office and not senators_expelled
subtitle: −2 political capital. The Office's files name the worst. The blocs that lose them will not forgive it.
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 2; Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.2, rim: 0.55, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.65, pal: 0.2, cis: 0.4}, true);
Q.ex_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['regulate', 'corruption']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Expulsion Resolution', Q.ex_vote);
if (Q.ex_vote >= 50) {
    Q.senators_expelled = 1; Q.corruption -= 10; Q.faith += 3;
    Q.guild_relation -= 8; Q.pal_relation -= 6; Q.rim_relation -= 4;
    for (var i = 0; i < SW.REGIONS.length; i++) { Q[SW.REGIONS[i] + '_guild'] *= 0.92; Q[SW.REGIONS[i] + '_pal'] *= 0.95; }
    SW.computeSupport(Q);
}
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if senators_expelled : For the first time since the Ruusan Reformation, the Senate expels its own. Eleven senators are escorted from the rotunda by the Senate Guard, among them two guild delegates and a member of the Chancellor's own bloc. Their worlds will send new senators. Their former colleagues will remember who brought the motion. ?][? if not senators_expelled : The motion fails. The accused senators vote on their own expulsion, and so do their friends. ?]

@oversight_act
view-if: intel_runs >= 1 and not intel_oversight
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Bureau of Intelligence would answer to the Senate's committee, not the Chancellery.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1; Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.45, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.3, ind: 0.65, pal: 0.1, cis: 0.5}, true);
Q.io_act_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Intelligence Oversight Act', Q.io_act_vote);
if (Q.io_act_vote >= 50) { Q.intel_oversight = 1; Q.evidence += 0.5; Q.bureau_relation += 5; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if intel_oversight : The Senate Bureau of Intelligence will report to the Judiciary & Intelligence Committee, and its director will testify to it in closed session every quarter. ?][? if not intel_oversight : The act fails. ?]

@compor
view-if: intel_oversight and not compor
subtitle: −2 political capital. A Senate commission against subversion: schemes foreseen, proof kept safe, investigators protected.
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 2; Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.4, rim: 0.55, sec: 0.5, ind: 0.6, pal: 0.2, cis: 0.3}, true);
Q.cp_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Commission for the Protection of the Republic', Q.cp_vote);
if (Q.cp_vote >= 50) { Q.compor = 1; Q.evidence_secured = 1; Q.senate_resolve += 0.5; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if compor : The Commission for the Protection of the Republic opens its offices beside the Bureau's. Its investigators answer to a cross-bench panel of senators, and its first act is to put every witness and analyst of the Senate's inquiries under its protection. ?][? if not compor : The commission is voted down. ?]

@gunray
view-if: gunray_stage >= 1 and gunray_stage <= 4 and not gunray_convicted
subtitle: Strengthens the prosecution at the next trial.
on-arrival: gunray_bonus += 1

The Judiciary Committee assigns its best prosecutors to the Gunray case and shields the witnesses.

@warrant
view-if: evidence >= 7 and not warrant
subtitle: [? if evidence >= 8 : Our evidence can justify a warrant. ?][? if evidence < 8 : We need a little more before a judge will sign. ?]
choose-if: evidence >= 8
unavailable-subtitle: Needs compelling evidence (8+).
on-arrival: warrant = 1; senate_resolve += 0.5

A sealed warrant is drafted and signed by three justices of the Supreme Court. It names no one yet. It does not need to. If the moment comes, the Jedi will be acting for the Senate, not against it.

@bureau_reform
view-if: bureau_reform_timer <= 0 and bureau_relation < 70 and not bureau_reformed
subtitle: −1 political capital. Clears out the guilds' placemen: the bureaucracy warms to us considerably, the guilds less so.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; bureau_relation += 30; bureau_dossier = 0; guild_relation -= 5; inst_dissent -= 3; bureau_reform_timer = 6; bureau_reviewed = 1; judiciary_timer = 1

The Committee audits the Senate's payroll. Forty officials on retainer to the Trade Federation are quietly retired; their replacements owe their jobs to the reform. For a while, at least, the Caucus's bills reach the floor on time.

@civil_service
view-if: bureau_reviewed and not bureau_reformed
subtitle: −1 political capital. A permanent, independent civil service, if the Senate agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.25, rim: 0.65, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.2, cis: 0.3}, true);
Q.cs_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Civil Service Act', Q.cs_vote);
if (Q.cs_vote >= 50) { Q.bureau_reformed = 1; Q.bureau_relation = Math.max(Q.bureau_relation, 60); Q.bureau_dossier = 0; Q.guild_relation -= 4; Q.faith += 1; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if bureau_reformed : The Civil Service Act passes. Appointments to the Senate's permanent staff will be made on merit and reviewed in public, and no official may take a fee from a bloc or a guild. The men and women who ran the Republic from its back offices now answer to it. ?][? if not bureau_reformed : The bill dies on the floor. The back offices of the Senate go on as before, and they will remember who tried. ?]

@amedda
view-if: bureau_reformed and not amedda_arrested and not amedda_removed and not sidious_defeated and not sidious_fled
subtitle: −1 political capital. The new civil service has opened the Vice Chair's files.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and evidence >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: [? if evidence < 3 : We need more evidence before we can move against him. ?][? if evidence >= 3 : Needs 1 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1; Q.amedda_arrested = 1; Q.vice_chair = 'Ask Aak';
Q.evidence += 1.5; Q.grand_plan -= 2; Q.pal_relation -= 10; Q.senate_resolve += 0.5;
for (var i = 0; i < SW.REGIONS.length; i++) Q[SW.REGIONS[i] + '_rc'] += 2;
SW.momentum(Q, 0.6, 'the arrest of Mas Amedda');
Q.scheme_timer = 0;
SW.clearSuspect(Q, 'amedda', 'arrest');
SW.computeSupport(Q);
!}
achievement: amedda

Senate Guards walk into the Vice Chair's office at dawn. The files the reformed civil service found in his archive are laid out on his desk: bills ruled out of order for money, appointments sold, a private line to the Chancellery that no one could explain. Mas Amedda says nothing at all. The Senate elects Ask Aak of Malastare to the gavel, and for the first time in years the Caucus's bills are heard. Somewhere, someone is very angry.

@integrity
view-if: anti_corruption and not integrity_office
subtitle: −1 political capital. A permanent office to audit every senator, if the Senate agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and guild_hold = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if guild_hold > 0 : The guilds whose money we took will not allow it. ?][? if guild_hold = 0 : Needs 1 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.1, rim: 0.7, sec: 0.4, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.3, cis: 0.3}, true);
Q.io_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', 'regulate', 'corruption']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Office of Public Integrity Act', Q.io_vote);
if (Q.io_vote >= 50) { Q.integrity_office = 1; Q.corruption -= 3; Q.faith += 1; Q.guild_relation -= 4; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if integrity_office : The Office of Public Integrity opens on the lowest floor of the Senate Building, with a staff of auditors who cannot be fired by the people they audit. Votes are no longer for sale, or at least no longer cheap. ?][? if not integrity_office : The Office is voted down. Too many senators would have had to explain their accounts. ?]

@hhc_investigate
view-if: not hhc_investigated
subtitle: −1 political capital. Follow the money behind the human-first movement.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; hhc_investigated = 1; evidence += 0.3; fear -= 1; judiciary_timer = 1

The Bureau of Intelligence follows the credits behind the human-first rallies on Coruscant and Corulag. They lead to shipping magnates, to retired admirals, and to a charity whose board meets at the Chancellery. The report is careful, and damning.

@syndicates
view-if: pirates_crushed and not syndicates_broken and not hutt_deal
subtitle: −1 political capital. Go after the Hutt cartels and Black Sun themselves.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.judiciary_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
Q.syndicate_tries = (Q.syndicate_tries || 0) + 1;
var p = SW.clamp(0.45 + Q.judicial_forces * 0.04 + Q.evidence * 0.02 + (Q.integrity_office ? 0.1 : 0) + Q.syndicate_tries * 0.08, 0.3, 0.9);
Q.syndicates_ok = Math.random() < p ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.syndicates_ok) {
    Q.syndicates_broken = 1; Q.corruption -= 8; Q.faith += 2; Q.rim_hardship -= 3;
    for (var i = 0; i < SW.REGIONS.length; i++) Q[SW.REGIONS[i] + '_rc'] += 2.5;
    SW.momentum(Q, 0.8, 'breaking the syndicates'); this.achieve('syndicates');
    SW.computeSupport(Q);
} else { Q.corruption += 1; SW.momentum(Q, -0.3, 'a failed raid on the syndicates'); }
!}

[? if syndicates_ok : Judicial task forces, backed by the patrol fleets, raid the counting houses of Nal Hutta and the Black Sun vigos' towers on Coruscant's lower levels in a single night. A hundred senators wake to find their benefactors in custody. The HoloNet calls it the end of an age, and for once the HoloNet is right. ?][? if not syndicates_ok : The raids are betrayed: the vigos are gone hours before the task forces arrive, and the cartels' lawyers are on the HoloNet by morning. We will have to try again. ?]

@patronage_1
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_judiciary = 1
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Core Worlds. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'judiciary', 'rc', 1); !}

A dozen vacant judgeships in Coruscant's courts go to lawyers from families that have always voted for the Caucus. They are not the best candidates. Their families are very grateful, and so are the Core Worlds' great houses that recommended them.

@patronage_2
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_judiciary = 2
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Colonies and the Inner Rim. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'judiciary', 'rc', 2); !}

The committee's investigators decide that the cases against three senators from the Colonies, all of whom vote with the Caucus, lack sufficient evidence. The files are sealed. Their delegations will remember the favour.

@patronage_3
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_judiciary = 3
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Mid Rim and the Expansion Region. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'judiciary', 'rc', 3); !}

The Republic's intelligence services need listening posts along the Mid Rim, and the committee leases them from worlds whose senators vote with us, at rents nobody else would pay. The posts hear very little. Their landlords hear the Caucus's name with fondness.

@patronage_4
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_judiciary = 4
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Outer Rim. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'judiciary', 'rc', 4); !}

A dozen vacant sector magistracies on the Outer Rim go to the nominees of friendly governors. The new magistrates know little law, but a great deal about who appointed them. Their sectors' delegations vote accordingly.

@patronage_5
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_judiciary = 5
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Mid Rim and the Expansion Region. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'judiciary', 'rc', 5); !}

The charges against two shipping magnates of the Hydian Way, for smuggling, bribery and creative bookkeeping, are dropped for want of a witness willing to testify. Their companies employ half the voters of three Mid Rim sectors, and those sectors' senators are very grateful.

@patronage_6
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_judiciary = 6
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Core Worlds. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'judiciary', 'rc', 6); !}

The Bureau of Intelligence's contracts for slicers, analysts and secure couriers go to Coruscant firms owned by families that support the Caucus. The work is middling. The invoices are excellent.
